  "goodToKnow": "Unantastbar means inviolable or untouchable. The most famous sentence in German law is the first of the Grundgesetz (1949): Die Würde des Menschen ist unantastbar. The so-called eternity clause (Article 79(3)) protects this principle from any constitutional amendment. Of people, unantastbar means beyond criticism or reach. From antasten (to touch, infringe)."
